Thanks for the suggestion Garett! I didn't know about mapply. I had been under the assumption you always had to specify a matrix or data frame for apply to work on. I look forward to using mapply in the future to get rid of all my loops. For reference here is what I ended up with after I took your suggestion. For me, I assume my column names contain my variable names so I don't need a list of them. When I ran them through microbenchmark on a scale with 120 items the loop took an average of 21.2 seconds and the apply statements took an average of 9 seconds for the IIFs and 11 seconds for the ICCs. Overall I guess it was only a 1 second time save but on larger scales it's going to really add up.

